[agent:result] ===BATCH===
[agent:result] Usage: hops batch [OPTIONS]
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Run a batch of ``hops`` commands in one process against one connection.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Reads newline-separated ``hops`` commands (each WITHOUT the leading
[agent:result]   ``hops``, though a leading ``hops`` is tolerated) from FILE or, when no
[agent:result]   ``-f`` is given, from stdin. Blank lines and lines starting with ``#`` are
[agent:result]   skipped. The SDK login performed by the first command that needs it is
[agent:result]   reused by the rest, so a 10-step feature pipeline pays one login instead of
[agent:result]   ten.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Example::
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]       hops batch <<'EOF'     fg create txns --primary-key id --event-time ts
[agent:result]       --online     fg insert txns --file txns.csv     fv create txns_fv
[agent:result]       --query "SELECT * FROM txns"     EOF
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   Args:     ctx: Click context (unused; each line builds its own root
[agent:result]   context).     script_file: Optional path to read commands from instead of
[agent:result]   stdin.     stop_on_error: When True, stop at the first command that fails.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result] Options:
[agent:result]   -f, --file FILE         Read commands from this file instead of stdin.
[agent:result]   --stop-on-error         Abort at the first failing command (default: keep
[agent:result]                           going).
[agent:result]   --json                  Output as JSON (machine-readable; for LLMs and
[agent:result]                           scripts).
[agent:result]   --verify / --no-verify  Verify the Hopsworks TLS certificate; --no-verify
[agent:result]                           skips verification for self-signed / IP-SAN-
[agent:result]                           mismatched certs.
[agent:result]   -h, --help              Show this message and exit.
